      "comment": "CHIEF OF WAR (8) progressive gelding who tackled the mile for the first time with a gritty second at Corowa in decent time. Blinkers go on in this stronger contest and has genuine winning claims. SPREAD THE LOVE (7) saves his best for this track and looks ready for the 1600m. Ran fifth in a bunched finish over 1300m at Goulburn second up. Will hold a forward position and looks right in this. MIDNIGHT AFFAIR (6) had been in sparkling form winning three races on end, before jumping in grade from the wide gate with a plugging eighth over 1600m at Kembla Grange. Don't underestimate from the good gate. ROCCO LINI (2) massive jump in grade from the wide barrier with a tiring last over 1550m at Canterbury in BM72 company. Has won over the 1800m here and no excuses from the rails draw.",
